      "writtenOn": "2026-01-20T20:00:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this can become a `compare_exchange` if we do remove the `HostMappedPersistent` state.\n\nSeparately, I was also thinking that maybe the state change could actually happen in the ctor of the `ScopedUseBuffer`. I don\u0027t have a strong preference for this, but right now, only the dtor does anything for that thing and it\u0027s sort of requiring the user to do something before which doesn\u0027t feel as RAII as what the class suggests.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 661,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 661,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "0602454cf72344c526fb8ad25df86fa4fa0183f1",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f02bd88_627cd405",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Buffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 661,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-21T18:51:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think this can become a compare_exchange if we do remove the HostMappedPersistent state.\n\nThat is possible but it becomes:\n\n```\nauto state \u003d BufferState::Unmapped;\nbool compare \u003d compare_exchange_strong(state, BufferState::InsideOperation, ...);\nDAWN_CHECK(compare);\n```\n\nSince execution stops if compare fails we don\u0027t gain anything by comparing before the exchange happens vs after? Comparing after using exchange() seemed simpler as a result.\n\n\u003e Separately, I was also thinking that maybe the state change could actually happen in the ctor of the ScopedUseBuffer. I don\u0027t have a strong preference for this, but right now, only the dtor does anything for that thing and it\u0027s sort of requiring the user to do something before which doesn\u0027t feel as RAII as what the class suggests.\n\nWe can\u0027t do the compare exchange in the constructor if we use it from the queue for external API usage. The constructor can\u0027t fail and return an error which is required. I did make ScopedUseBuffer only able to be constructed from BufferBase though to hopefully prevent misuse.",
      "parentUuid": "c3732ce5_809a2437",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 661,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 661,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "0602454cf72344c526fb8ad25df86fa4fa0183f1",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a16b0b02_edde4927",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Buffer.cpp",
